    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "SonicBuds feature a 30g magnesium alloy body with a matte black finish, a 3-axis accelerometer for auto-pause, a bone-conduction sensor for ambient monitoring, and a dedicated call button with haptic feedback. AudioFlow uses a 28g polycarbonate shell with a glossy white finish, a single-microphone directional array, a 2-axis tilt sensor, and a physical inline remote with a volume rocker. SonicBuds supports LDAC, AAC, and aptX HD codecs with a 0.5W wireless charging case, while AudioFlow offers SBC and AAC only with a 0.2W wired charging case. Both include a 3.5mm aux output, but SonicBuds adds a USB-C to Lightning adapter and a 40mm dynamic driver, whereas AudioFlow has a 12mm balanced armature driver and a proprietary micro-USB port. SonicBuds features a dual-battery case with a blue LED indicator ring, while AudioFlow uses a single-battery case with a red LED status dot. SonicBuds includes a silicone ear tip set in S/M/L sizes with a 45-degree angle, while AudioFlow offers foam tips in S",
